sagreeing with the body's envelope claim (or\nsrc/shared/inboundClassification.ts:208: * with the body's classification), and the `Mcp-Method` header disagreeing\nsrc/shared/inboundClassification.ts:323:            'SEP-2243 standard `Mcp-Method` / `Mcp-Name` headers — presence, sentinel decoding, and `Mcp-Name` ↔ body cross-check ' +\nsrc/shared/inboundClassification.ts:325:            'dispatch. The classifier’s own header-mismatch cells (protocol-version, `Mcp-Method` mismatch) stay on the edge ' +\nsrc/shared/inboundClassification.ts:326:            '`era-classification` rung; this rung carries the entry-layer presence/`Mcp-Name` half. Evaluated before the ' +\nsrc/shared/inboundClassification.ts:458: * `Mcp-Name` header must mirror, and which body field supplies it (SEP-2243\nsrc/shared/inboundClassification.ts:475: * `era-classification` rung for the `MCP-Protocol-Version` and\nsrc/shared/inboundClassification.ts:476: * `Mcp-Method` *mismatch* cells) when:\nsrc/shared/inboundClassification.ts:478: * - the required `Mcp-Method` header is absent;\nsrc/shared/inboundClassification.ts:479: * - the required `Mcp-Name` header is absent on a `tools/call`,\nsrc/shared/inboundClassification.ts:482: * - the `Mcp-Name` header carries an invalid `=?base64?…?=` sentinel; or\nsrc/shared/inboundClassification.ts:483: * - the (decoded) `Mcp-Name` value disagrees with the body's\nsrc/shared/inboundClassification.ts:487: * \"All requests\"), for methods that have no `Mcp-Name` source, and when the\nsrc/shared/inboundClassification.ts:494: * function is the presence/`Mcp-Name` half of the standard-header rung the\nsrc/shared/inboundClassification.ts:507:            `the body names method ${method} but the required Mcp-Method header is absent`,\nsrc/shared/inboundClassification.ts:535:            `the body carries params.${sourceField}=\"${bodyValue}\" but the required Mcp-Name header is absent`,\nsrc/shared/inboundClassification.ts:545:            'the Mcp-Name header carries an invalid Base64 sentinel value',\nsrc/shared/inboundClassification.ts:553:            `the body carries params.${sourceField}=\"${bodyValue}\" but the Mcp-Name header names \"${decoded}\"`,\nsrc/shared/inboundClassification.ts:662:                'an initialize request (legacy handshake) was sent with a modern MCP-Protocol-Version header'\nsrc/shared/inboundClassification.ts:696:                `the body envelope names protocol version ${claimedVersion} but the MCP-Protocol-Version header names ${headerVersion}`\nsrc/shared/inboundClassification.ts:703:                `the body names method ${method} but the Mcp-Method header names ${request.mcpMethodHeader}`\nsrc/shared/inboundClassification.ts:727:                `Invalid params: the MCP-Protocol-Version header names protocol revision ${headerVersion}, but the request is missing ` +\nsrc/shared/inboundClassification.ts:775:                `the notification envelope names protocol version ${claimedVersion} but the MCP-Protocol-Version header names ${headerVersion}`\nsrc/shared/inboundClassification.ts:783:                `the notification body names method ${method} but the Mcp-Method header names ${request.mcpMethodHeader}`\nsrc/shared/inboundClassification.ts:792:    // keeps it legacy traffic. The Mcp-Method header is validated only when\nsrc/shared/inboundClassification.ts:800:                `the notification body names method ${method} but the Mcp-Method header names ${request.mcpMethodHeader}`\nsrc/shared/mcpParamHeaders.ts:11: * The standard-header half (`MCP-Protocol-Version`, `Mcp-Method`, `Mcp-Name`)\nsrc/types/spec.types.2026-07-28.ts:78:     * For the HTTP transport, this value MUST match the `MCP-Protocol-Version`\nsrc/wire/rev2026-07-28/schemas.ts:633:     * the value must match the `MCP-Protocol-Version` header.\nsrc/types/constants.ts:17: * For the HTTP transport, the value must match the `MCP-Protocol-Version` header.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
